格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Kimi WebBridge for DeepSeek Harness — a third-party dsh plugin bundle that turns the local Kimi WebBridge daemon into 15 native kimi_webbridge_* browser tools (navigate, click, fill, snapshot, screenshot, evaluate, network, upload, PDF).","id":"gh:1333726561","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-Kimi-WebBridge","slug":"MicroHEROX/dsh-Kimi-WebBridge","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins","kimi"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Kimi WebBridge for DeepSeek Harness — a third-party dsh plugin bundle that turns the local Kimi WebB"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ridge daemon into 15 native kimi_webbridge_* browser tools (navigate, click, fill, snapshot, screens"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"hot, evaluate, network, upload, PDF)."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# Kimi WebBridge for DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Give your DeepSeek Harness agents the user's real browser — with their login sessions.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"*A third-party plugin bundle for DeepSeek Harness (dsh). It turns the local Kimi WebBridge daemon in"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"to 15 native `kimi_webbridge_*` tools — the agent can open pages, read them, click, type, screenshot"},{"id":"p4s3","text":", run JS, inspect network traffic, upload files, and save PDFs in **your real browser**, logged in a"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"S, inspect network traffic, upload files, and save PDFs in **your real browser**, logged in as you.*"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## ✨ What it does"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"| 🧭 **Real browser, real sessions** | The model drives your actual browser — cookies, logins and all"},{"id":"p6s2","text":". No scraping, no headless shell. |\n| 🛡️ **Local-only** | Everything happens on your machine: plugin"},{"id":"p6s3","text":" → `127.0.0.1:10086` daemon → your browser. No third-party service sees your traffic. |\n| 📦 **One fi"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"le, no build** | Pure ESM, zero runtime dependencies beyond the harness's own packages. No TypeScrip"},{"id":"p6s5","text":"t, no transpile, no API keys. |\n| 🔌 **Standard Cordis bundle** | `name` / `inject` / `apply` + `defi"},{"id":"p6s6","text":"neTool` — the exact pattern the shipped harness tools use. Never touches the dsh installation. |\n| 🗂"},{"id":"p6s7","text":"️ **Tab groups like the product** | One session = one tab group; the model names the group in your l"},{"id":"p6s8","text":"anguage on first use and closes it only when you ask. |"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## 🛠️ What the model gets — 15 tools"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"| Tool | Purpose |"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| `kimi_webbridge_navigate` | Open a URL (new tab or current), set the tab-group label on first use "},{"id":"p9s2","text":"|\n| `kimi_webbridge_find_tab` | Re-select a task tab by URL; `active:true` borrows the tab you're vi"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"ewing |\n| `kimi_webbridge_list_tabs` | List the task's tabs |\n| `kimi_webbridge_snapshot` | Read the"},{"id":"p9s4","text":" page as an accessibility tree with `@e` element refs |\n| `kimi_webbridge_click` | Click an element "},{"id":"p9s5","text":"(`@e` ref or CSS selector) |\n| `kimi_webbridge_fill` | Type into inputs, textareas and contenteditab"},{"id":"p9s6","text":"le rich editors |\n| `kimi_webbridge_evaluate` | Run JavaScript in the page (async supported) |\n| `ki"},{"id":"p9s7","text":"mi_webbridge_cdp` | Raw `chrome.debugger` passthrough (advanced escape hatch) |\n| `kimi_webbridge_sc"},{"id":"p9s8","text":"reenshot` | Screenshot the tab or one element; returns a file path |\n| `kimi_webbridge_network` | Ca"},{"id":"p9s9","text":"pture / inspect the tab's network requests |\n| `kimi_webbridge_upload` | Upload files to a `<input t"},{"id":"p9s10","text":"ype=file>` |\n| `kimi_webbridge_save_as_pdf` | Render the current page to PDF; returns a file path |\n"},{"id":"p9s11","text":"| `kimi_webbridge_close_tab` | Close the current tab |\n| `kimi_webbridge_close_session` | Close the "},{"id":"p9s12","text":"whole tab group — only when you ask |\n| `kimi_webbridge_start_daemon` | Auto-start the local daemon "},{"id":"p9s13","text":"only when you ask |\n| `kimi_webbridge_start_daemon` | Auto-start the local daemon when unreachable |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## ✅ Requirements & versions"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| Component | Version |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| DeepSeek Harness (`dsh`) | **0.1.0-rc.8 / 0.1.1-rc.1** (tested) — any build shipping `@deepseek-ai"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"/dsh-tools` should work |\n| Node.js | **≥ 18** (global `fetch`) |\n| Kimi WebBridge daemon | **v1.11."},{"id":"p12s3","text":"5** (tested) |\n| Kimi WebBridge browser extension | **1.11.5** (tested) |\n| OS | **Windows** (tested"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"); macOS/Linux supported by code paths, not yet verified |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"> Compatibility is pinned to what was actually verified. Run `node tests/smoke.mjs` after installing"},{"id":"p13s2","text":" to check your environment."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## 📦 Installation"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"**Option A — from GitHub (recommended):**"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"**Option B — from a local checkout:**"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"**Option C — no install, one-off overlay** (`kimi-webbridge.overlay.yml`):"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"**Option D — permanent merge:** copy the `insert` block from `cordis.patch.yml` into `$DSH_HOME/prof"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"iles/<name>/cordis.patch.yml` (or `$DSH_HOME/cordis.patch.yml` for all profiles)."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"**Uninstall:**"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"The CLI removes the dependency and reconciles the profile's layer list; the 15 tools unregister. Ver"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"ify the row is gone:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"> ⚠️ **Known harness caveat (dsh 0.1.0-rc.8, discussion #913):** on rare transient pnpm failures the"},{"id":"p27s2","text":" entry can remain in `dsh.profile.bundles`, and the profile then fails to boot with `cannot resolve "},{"id":"p27s3","text":"profile bundle \"dsh-kimi-webbridge\"` — `dsh plugin install` does **not** fix it (community analysis:"},{"id":"p27s4","text":" #917). **Recovery:** edit the profile's `package.json` and delete `\"dsh-kimi-webbridge\"` from `dsh."},{"id":"p27s5","text":"profile.bundles`, then boot again."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"> Only runtime files (`index.js`, `cordis.patch.yml`, READMEs, LICENSE) are installed; `docs/` and `"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"tests/` stay in this repository. Verified with `npm pack`."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## 🚀 Quick start"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"1. Install the bundle and start `dsh web --profile demo`.\n2. Wait for the `kimi_webbridge_*` tools i"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"n the catalog.\n3. Ask: *\"Open example.com in the browser, tell me what's on the page, and screenshot"},{"id":"p30s3","text":" it.\"*\n4. The agent opens a tab group (named in your language), reads the page via `snapshot`, saves"},{"id":"p30s4","text":" the screenshot, and shows you the file."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"## ⚙️ Configuration"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"All keys optional; override the `kimi-webbridge` row from a later patch layer, restating every key y"},{"id":"p32s2","text":" optional; override the `kimi-webbridge` row from a later patch layer, restating every key you need:"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## 🔐 Security"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"- The daemon listens on `127.0.0.1` only; the model operates your browser **as you**. Review what yo"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"ur harness is allowed to ask for.\n- The plugin stores and sends **no credentials**, has **no filesys"},{"id":"p35s3","text":"tem access**, and never modifies the `deepseek-harness` installation.\n- `kimi_webbridge_cdp` and `ki"},{"id":"p35s4","text":"mi_webbridge_evaluate` are powerful; disable them for untrusted model policies."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"## 📌 Version & compatibility"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"- **Plugin:** 0.1.0\n- **Tested with:** dsh 0.1.0-rc.8 / 0.1.1-rc.1 · Node 24 (≥18 required) · Kimi W"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"ebBridge daemon v1.11.5 / extension 1.11.5 · Windows\n- **Dependencies:** none declared — `@deepseek-"},{"id":"p37s3","text":"ai/dsh-tools` resolves at runtime from the harness installation (no registry copies are installed)"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
